From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ThaRae <76752281+ThaRae@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:44:50 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Tests: Allow a link hover in a navigated iframe before the
 next move

When the iframe navigates under the resting pointer, a rendering update
of its new document can hover the link under the pointer before the
test checks that the outgoing document's hover ended. Accept that
report there, as the hover the next move would otherwise give.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Tests/LibWebView/TestLinkHoverStatus.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Tests/LibWebView/TestLinkHoverStatus.cpp b/Tests/LibWebView/TestLinkHoverStatus.cpp
index 23631c5edc88b348242cfa6bcf058d96b68d108f..5e8c3795595981e773505f486a726ec142f58273 100644
--- a/Tests/LibWebView/TestLinkHoverStatus.cpp
+++ b/Tests/LibWebView/TestLinkHoverStatus.cpp
@@ -160,7 +160,7 @@ function navigate_frame() { frame.srcdoc = frame.getAttribute("srcdoc") + "<!--
     VERIFY(hovered_url->serialize() == "https://example.com/in-iframe"sv);
     view->run_javascript("navigate_frame()"_string);
     Core::EventLoop::current().spin_until([&]() { return unhovers_reported >= 6; });
-    VERIFY(!hovered_url.has_value());
+    VERIFY(!hovered_url.has_value() || hovers_reported == 7);
     Core::EventLoop::current().spin_until([&]() { return last_title == "frame load 2"sv; });
 
     // The new iframe document's link is a fresh target. Then over to the page's own link: The iframe's handler hears
